    75	`f_N(x') = f_N(x)` whenever `x' ≡ x (mod 2^{k−3})`. So `s mod 2^k` is a function of `(N mod 2^k, p mod 2^{k−3})`.
    76	*Proof.* `f(x') − f(x) = (x' − x)(1 − N/(xx'))`. `x' ≡ x (mod 8)` gives `xx' ≡ x² ≡ 1 ≡ N (mod 8)`, so the second factor is
